  <section>
    <div class="wide">
      {{> components/pattern-examples topic="connection-failover"}}
      <p>Say your invoice worker uses your primary relay, A, and you've approved a secondary relay, B.
        If A can't open a usable connection, B can take the send. New work returns to A when it recovers, and your worker keeps calling the primary Mailer.</p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>A connection fails before submission.</strong> An eligible failure can send the job to the backup relay.</li>
        <li><strong>The server temporarily refuses the whole send.</strong> A separate <a href="/mail-send-retries.html">retry policy</a>
          can try again on the selected destination. A started submission stays on its selected relay. If the final reply goes missing, that relay
          may already have accepted the message.</li>
        <li><strong>A healthy pool is full.</strong> The send waits in the usual way. See <a href="/smtp-connection-pooling.html">pool and cluster configuration</a>
          to distribute ordinary load.</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </section>
